--- !u!114 &3351795647594245741
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2498330608265881580}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d85e0dc8a5f3b3d47bddeb04441c359a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NpcTalk
  npcName: Bram
  nameColor: {r: 0.54901963, g: 0.24313726, b: 0.14901961, a: 1}
  firstVisit:
  - Name's Bram. I keep the forge, and the Village Fund along with it.
  - 'Bring back Motion Shards and we''ll put them toward fixing up Alderbrook: the
    well, the lamps, Mira''s garden, the old shrine.'
  - Talk to me again and I'll open the ledger. Every shard you bring home goes on
    the page.
  partsFound:
  - Wren's got {parts} of those old parts on his table now. Heavy as anything.
  - Whoever built them knew a thing or two about momentum.
  idle:
  - A heavy crate is slow to start and slow to stop. Same with stubborn blacksmiths.
  - Push the same crate together and your forces add. Two of you shove twice as hard
    as one.
  bubbleOffset: {x: 0, y: 2.7}
  closeDistance: 3.5
  opensVillageFund: 1
  homecoming:
  - So the old engine roared back to life. Felt it in my anvil, I did.
  - The heavier and the faster, the harder to stop. You two proved it. Now, about
    that ledger...
  afterRegion:
  - Whatever shards are left in your pockets, the village can still use them.
  - Heavy cart, long fall, big hit. I'll be telling that story for years.
  creditsAfterHomecoming: 0
